# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Node
#
# node_modules is ~150 packages of small files and is needed ONLY to rebuild the
# interface. The server never reads it -- FiveM serves the built output in
# br_ui/ui/ as static files.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
.npm/
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DO NOT IGNORE br_ui/ui/
#
# This is the opposite of the usual rule, so it is spelled out: ui/ is BUILD
# OUTPUT and it is COMMITTED ON PURPOSE. fxmanifest.lua serves those files
# directly, and there is deliberately no build step on the server. Adding ui/ to
# this file would produce a server that starts cleanly and shows a blank screen,
# which is a genuinely annoying thing to debug.
#
# After changing anything under br_ui/src/, run `npm run build` and commit the
# regenerated ui/ alongside the source change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
!resources/[fivem-royale]/br_ui/ui/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets and per-host configuration
#
# server.cfg holds the Cfx.re license key, the database password and admin
# identifiers. Track server.cfg.example instead and keep the real one local.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
server.cfg
# The live dev/public tunables, exec'd by server.cfg. Per-host by definition --
# it is the file whose whole job is to differ between the dev box and the public
# one -- so the box keeps its own and the repo tracks the two examples it is
# copied from: tunables.dev.cfg.example and tunables.public.cfg.example.
tunables.cfg
*.env
.env*

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# FXServer runtime
#
# If the repo is ever cloned directly into a server directory, these are the
# things the server generates and should never be tracked.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
cache/
logs/
*.log
svadhesive/
citizen/
alpine/
run.sh
FXServer*
server-data/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Session working memory
#
# PLAN.md is the living handoff document between working sessions -- project
# state, testing strategy, what's next. It is deliberately untracked: the repo
# documents the project, PLAN.md documents the work in progress.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
PLAN.md

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors and OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
.DS_Store

# Local editor/agent state. Nothing in here is part of the game or the build,
# and the paths inside it are machine-specific. Ignored as a whole rather than
# per-subdirectory because of `.claude/worktrees/`: each worktree is a full
# checkout carrying its own `.git` file, which `git add -A` happily commits as
# an embedded repo. That has already happened here once.
.claude/
